  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn ichidan verb with two distinct meanings. Sense 1 (reform/revise) is the more common meaning in everyday use. Sense 2 (examine/inspect) appears in formal or official contexts. The adverb {改|あらた}めて means \"again, anew, afresh\" and is extremely common in both spoken and written Japanese.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {態度|たいど}を{改|あらた}める: to reform one's attitude\n- {名前|なまえ}を{改|あらた}める: to change one's name\n- {改|あらた}めて: again, afresh, anew\n- {改|あらた}めてお{礼|れい}を{申|もう}し{上|あ}げます: I would like to express my thanks once again (formal)\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {改|かい} appears in many compound words related to change and revision: {改善|かいぜん} (improvement), {改革|かいかく} (reform), {改正|かいせい} (amendment).",
